    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc85877c_40f2aa19",
        "filename": "compos/aidl/com/android/virt/compos/ICompService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-16T17:31:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree. This is not yet a general enough solution for running an executable from an APK.  However, I still think the service should not open to run any executable by default.  This service itself is a big attack surface, and the developer shouldn\u0027t assume the input comes from them (although I think ideally they should be able to assume so, but it seems to be a current limitation).  So we might need a way for the app developer to configure the service somehow.\n\nTaking a step back, the SDK/API requirements are not clear to me.  We could support running executable(s) and/or native binder service(s), and the design may depend on what we really want to provide.  Also, we probably haven\u0027t thought about KeyMint for apps?\n\nSome early ideas to achieve what you want:\n * Make authfs support fd to a range within a file, e.g. an uncompressed executable in an APK may just look like an executable over authfs.\n   * Or, a executable loader in the VM to run such binaries.\n * Need a config by the app developer for the service setup.\n   * Or probably better, a programming paradigm that the developer can follow.\n\nAnyway, there are a lot of fun ahead :)",
      "parentUuid": "55af01dd_2a79fb24",
